# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tests that run the Neat Dataflow backend (label `dataflow`;
# tests/CMakeLists.txt appends this file to TSAN_OPTIONS for them when SIMA_ENABLE_TSAN is on).
#
# Why: on AArch64 the Dataflow runtime returns a pool slot with inline assembly (`stsetl`, a
# release read-modify-write on the pool's free set: scheduler-dataflow
# src/dataflow/storage/free_mask_internal.h:292-297). TSan does not instrument inline assembly, so
# it never sees that release. Session::stop -> SessionState::stop_locked releases the pools
# (session.cpp:518-525), and TensorPool's destructor (tensor_pool.cpp:213-225) deletes the pool
# only after settled() has read every free-set word with acquire (free_mask_internal.h:223): the
# order exists in hardware, but TSan reports the accesses made before the slot's return as racing
# with the delete. Not a race.
#
# Evidence (H0 C4 report, c4.md finding F4): (1) a 30-line reproducer of the pattern
# (evidence/c4/tsan-probe/asmprobe.cpp) reports this race with `stsetl` and none with
# std::atomic::fetch_or(memory_order_release), on the DevKit (asmprobe-board.txt); (2) Core's TSan
# build against a scratch copy of the runtime whose free-set operations use std::atomic in TSan
# builds (evidence/c4/runtime-tsan-verify.diff, 3 lines; not applied to the runtime)
# ran unit_dataflow_twin_lifecycle_teardown_test 5 of 5 times with 0 warnings, where the stock
# build warned in 3 of 4 runs (evidence/c4/tsan-verify/).
#
# One entry per report signature. Each matches the runtime frame that made the earlier access;
# the other side of every report is `operator delete` of the TensorPool in
# simaai::dataflow::detail::SessionState::stop_locked, reached from Run::stop or Run::close.
# The entries match function names, inlined frames included, so the binaries need their symbol
# table and debug information (TSan's in-process symbolizer reads both): with a stripped
# libsima_neat.so the frame of entry 2 is inlined away and that report is not suppressed. A
# suppressed report is still symbolized: with all of libsima_neat's DWARF, the first one of a
# process costs about 5 s on the DevKit's A65, enough to break a test's timing bound.
#
# Remove an entry when the runtime uses std::atomic for these operations under TSan.

# 1. A slot returned to the free set by an application thread, in TensorPool::release_slot_
#    (tensor_pool.cpp:464-470; FreeMask::push, free_mask_internal.h:110, inlined): a pulled
#    message's last reference dropped, or a refused try_push's unpublished WriteLoan dropped in
#    DataflowRun::push_item (WriteLoan::reset_). Its reads come before the inline `stsetl` return.
race:simaai::dataflow::TensorPool::release_slot_

# 2. A push filling its slot: Core's DataflowRun::push_item reads the pool's slot size through
#    WriteLoan::bytes (write_loan.h:39-41) -> TensorPool::slot_bytes (tensor_pool.h:170), both
#    inlined, before the loan is published or returned; the slot's return to the free set is the
#    same inline-asm release.
race:simaai::dataflow::TensorPool::slot_bytes
